id: 1113
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1113, "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "data": {"id": "2883305c-2f6f-468d-b73a-ef1d7510ad45", "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "kind": "tool", "position": 1111, "revision": 1113, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Read", "input": "{\"file_path\": \"[workspace]\", \"offset\": 90, \"limit\": 25}", "status": "running", "tool_use_id": "call_09c39bfe19b44fe4a0464ec9"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:24:13.810209+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:24:14.476692+00:00"}}

id: 1115
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1115, "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "data": {"id": "2883305c-2f6f-468d-b73a-ef1d7510ad45", "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "kind": "tool", "position": 1111, "revision": 1115, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Read", "input": "{\"file_path\": \"[workspace]\", \"offset\": 90, \"limit\": 25}", "output": "90\t**Object and scope:** Energy dependence of experimental dipole matrix element (DME) magnitudes across 13 measured energies (22.5–48.4 eV), extracted from `dipole_matrix_elements_datasets.tsv`. Each energy block contains 7 rows × 6 columns of (l, m, Re, Im, errRe, errIm) values.\n91\t\n92\t**Relationship:** The maximum real-part magnitude (**Re_max**) decreases with photon energy at a slope of **−0.011/eV** (r = −0.48, p = 0.095). The trend is marginally significant at the 5% level. The strongest DME occurs at 31.0 eV (Re_max = 0.71) and the weakest at 48.4 eV (Re_max = 0.12). The imaginary-part maximum shows a weaker decreasing trend (slope = −0.003/eV, r = −0.32, p = 0.29).\n93\t\n94\t**Leave-one-out robustness:** All 13/13 leave-one-out slopes maintain the same negative sign, ranging from −0.014 to −0.006/eV (mean = −0.011, std = 0.002). This indicates the trend is driven by the overall energy span rather than any single outlier point.\n95\t\n96\t**Core quantitative result:** Re_max slope = −0.011/eV, r = −0.48, p = 0.095. LOO consistency: 13/13 same-sign slopes. Analysis unit: per-energy maximum |Re| across all (l,m) channels.\n97\t\n98\t**Supporting evidence:**\n99\t- `output/fig3_dme_magnitude.csv` — per-energy DME statistics\n100\t- `output/analysis_results.json` — trend parameters\n101\t- `output/deep_analysis_results.json` — LOO results\n102\t- `output/analysis_02_core_findings.py` — analysis code lines 180–230\n103\t- `output/analysis_04_deep.py` — LOO analysis\n104\t\n105\t**Alternative explanations:** (1) The decrease may reflect the expected physical behavior that dipole transitions weaken at higher photon energies as the photon wavelength becomes shorter than the atomic/molecular scale. (2) The marginal p-value (0.095) means the null hypothesis of no trend cannot be rejected at α = 0.05. (3) Non-linear models (e.g., 1/E scaling) may fit better than the linear model tested here.\n106\t\n107\t**Limitations:** The p-value of 0.095 does not meet conventional significance thresholds. Only 13 energy points limit statistical power. The DME blocks have different (l,m) channel structures at different energies, so Re_max may not track the same physical transition across all energies.\n108\t\n109\t**Falsification proposal:** If the decrease is physical (cross-section weakening), adding DME measurements at 50–60 eV should continue the downward trend. If the trend is dominated by a specific channel transition, controlling for (l,m) selection should reveal a flatter energy dependence.\n110\t\n111\t---\n112\t\n113\t## Finding 4: Wigner delay and eigenphase sum exhibit characteristic resonance signatures with zero crossings and inflection points\n114\t", "status": "completed", "is_async": false, "tool_use_id": "call_09c39bfe19b44fe4a0464ec9"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:24:13.810209+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:24:14.585236+00:00"}}

