data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1130, "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "data": {"id": "32d1705a-4199-4794-9788-4ed3b029fb12", "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "kind": "tool", "position": 1128, "revision": 1130, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Read", "input": "{\"file_path\": \"[workspace]\", \"limit\": 20, \"offset\": 98}", "status": "running", "tool_use_id": "call_67f4a0487168441e89a0155a"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:24:29.549415+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:24:30.134187+00:00"}}

id: 1132
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1132, "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "data": {"id": "32d1705a-4199-4794-9788-4ed3b029fb12", "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "kind": "tool", "position": 1128, "revision": 1132, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Read", "input": "{\"file_path\": \"[workspace]\", \"limit\": 20, \"offset\": 98}", "output": "98\t**Supporting evidence:**\n99\t- `output/fig3_dme_magnitude.csv` — per-energy DME statistics\n100\t- `output/independent_dme_results.json` — independent sub-agent replication (Re_max slope = −0.0112/eV, r² = 0.23, p = 0.095; LOO 13/13 same-sign slopes; max_abs_real at 22.5 eV = 0.456)\n101\t- `output/deep_analysis_results.json` — LOO results\n102\t- `output/analysis_02_core_findings.py` — analysis code lines 180–230\n103\t- `output/analysis_04_deep.py` — LOO analysis\n104\t\n105\t**Leave-one-out robustness:** All 13/13 leave-one-out slopes maintain the same negative sign, ranging from −0.014 to −0.006/eV (mean = −0.011, std = 0.002). This indicates the trend is driven by the overall energy span rather than any single outlier point. Independent sub-agent replication confirms the slope (−0.0112/eV), LOO consistency (13/13 same-sign), and per-energy values (max_abs_real = 0.456 at 22.5 eV, 0.124 at 48.4 eV).\n106\t\n107\t---\n108\t\n109\t## Finding 4: Wigner delay and eigenphase sum exhibit characteristic resonance signatures with zero crossings and inflection points\n110\t\n111\t**Object and scope:** Energy-dependent Wigner time delay (`0.5_Wigner_delay`, 296 points, 0.5–30.0 eKE), angle-averaged delay (`angle_averaged_delay`, 200 points), and eigenphase sum (`eigenphase_sum`, 50 points, 0.5–30.0 eV) from `phase_and_delay_curves_datasets.tsv`.\n112\t\n113\t**Relationship:** The Wigner delay spans **−21.71 as to +182.56 as**, with a pronounced peak at **eKE = 9.1 eV** (182.56 as) and a minimum at **eKE = 0.5 eV** (−21.71 as). Two zero crossings occur at **eKE ≈ 2.9 eV and 17.1 eV**. The derivative of the Wigner delay shows sign changes at eKE ≈ 9.0 eV and 23.5 eV, marking the peak and a subsequent decline.\n114\t\n115\tThe eigenphase sum increases monotonically from **−1.11 rad to +0.47 rad** over 0.5–30.0 eV, with two inflection points at **eKE ≈ 2.5 eV and 17.0 eV** (identified by sign changes in the second derivative). The initial rapid rise (derivative up to 0.14 rad/eV) slows after ~17 eV, consistent with saturation behavior.\n116\t\n117\tThe angle-averaged delay mirrors the Wigner delay shape: min = −104.09 as at 0.9 eV, max = 141.36 as at 8.6 eV.", "status": "completed", "is_async": false, "tool_use_id": "call_67f4a0487168441e89a0155a"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:24:29.549415+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:24:30.215846+00:00"}}

