id: 1170
event: message.updated
data: {"type": "message.updated", "sequence": 1170, "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "data": {"id": "e3001346-b922-46c8-92f3-26aca345abda", "run_id": "run_7d89fb6062b44bd8", "kind": "tool", "position": 1166, "revision": 1170, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "agent_call_id": null, "data": {"name": "Read", "input": "{\"file_path\": \"[workspace]\", \"limit\": 20, \"offset\": 145}", "output": "145\t\n146\tThe four findings paint a coherent picture of energy-dependent photoionization dynamics with resonance-like features:\n147\t\n148\t1. **Phase divergence** (Finding 1) and **angular coefficient structure** (Finding 2) both show that the 24–30 eV region is particularly active, with F20 reaching a local minimum at 24.8 eV and a local maximum at 27.9 eV, while phase disagreement begins accelerating above ~28 eV.\n149\t\n150\t2. **DME weakening** (Finding 3) at higher energies is consistent with the general trend toward smaller angular coefficients at high energy (F20 declining from ~1.4 to ~0.26 between 27.9 and 48.4 eV).\n151\t\n152\t3. **Wigner delay features** (Finding 4) in the 0.5–30 eV range align with the energy window where the most dramatic angular coefficient changes occur, suggesting the resonance structure drives both the time-delay and angular distribution phenomena.\n153\t\n154\t## Reproducibility\n155\t\n156\tAll analysis was performed using Python 3.11 with pandas, numpy, and scipy. The complete analysis pipeline consists of scripts in `output/`:\n157\t\n158\t1. `output/analysis_01_explore_data.py` — Data loading and structural exploration\n159\t2. `output/analysis_02_core_findings.py` — Core statistical tests (linear regression, sign-change detection, DME trends)\n160\t3. `output/analysis_03_figures.py` — Figure CSV generation and cross-comparisons\n161\t4. `output/analysis_04_deep.py` — Angle-resolved analysis, polynomial fitting, leave-one-out robustness\n162\t5. `output/analysis_fix_energy_alignment.py` — **Corrected** energy-grid alignment with cubic spline interpolation and perturbation analysis\n163\t\n164\tTo reproduce: run each script in sequence from the project root directory:", "status": "completed", "is_async": false, "tool_use_id": "call_83397834b5f746668eede1eb"}, "created_at": "2026-10-16T09:25:00.632846+00:00", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T09:25:01.303674+00:00"}}

